		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=14517#p14517"><![CDATA[
Very, very nice!<br>I've recompiled the demo to enable CUDA and increased the number of cubes to 4500 (10 by 10 by 45). Using this setting de framerate drops below 24 only a few times.<br>But I see no apparent performance increase between the CPU solver and the CUDA solver (same with CUDA integrator vs CPU integrator). Am i doing something wrong?<br>My hardware: Geforce GTX 260, Core2 Quad Q9550 2.83Ghz, 8Gb internal ram.<br><br>I assumed CUDA could outperform a CPU by 5 to 20 times ..<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5440">Micha</a> — Tue Jul 28, 2009 12:15 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
